Z||000000||SloPonti||08-08-2000||12:20 AM||||hey guys i just purchased a 81 jeep cj7 for my girlfriend to drive! we both love it! it came with a hard top and it features an automatic tranny and air conditioning which is kinda rare for a jeep! but i am looking to buy some parts like door locks and handles and little stuff like that! i know of the jc whitney catalogue! does anyone know of a site like this fiero forum where i can learn more about the jeep and find parts?<BR>thanks<BR>Rob Schacht||||reg||5
Z||000001||b lo 0||08-08-2000||09:58 AM||||I have a '90 Wrangler-nice to see another Jeep owner here-first off, my suggestion is go to Bestop and get a soft top-they make them so they go right onto the hardtop mounting points.  Trust me, it's much more fun with a soft top.  Actually, some of my Jeep buddies won't wave to hardtop drivers.  Anyways, the auto is a rare find.  Congrats.  My Wrangler has a 5 speed, and no air.  As for Jeep parts, get the Jeep catalog from JC Whitney.  Also, get a subscription to Four Wheeler.  That's about all I can tell ya.  Have fun Jeepin'!<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">     <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!<P><A HREF="http://clubs.excite.com/welcome/main?cid=.zXb1DJ1lsCL&aid=22&auth=" TARGET=_blank>Pontiac Fiero Owner's Club</A>-Pics, Videos and More-Or Post your Own||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||08-08-2000||11:11 AM||||Do a Web search on "Jeep". There is a lot of stuff out there. Jeeps are a lot of fun. You'll find that the more you drive it or ride in it, the more you'll want to. Not real comfy on long trips, though.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>When I die, I want to go peacefully, in my sleep, like Grandpa.<BR>Not screaming, like the passengers in his car.||||reg||10
Z||000003||Monkeyman||08-08-2000||02:48 PM||||Here's a pic of the '79 CJ5 I used to have.  I've owned a couple of 7s, too.  The 7s are better on the road since they have a longer wheelbase, but the 5s are better for off roading.  Less wheelbase =  better maneuverability.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/'79JeepCJ5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||b lo 0||08-08-2000||04:08 PM||||I'll be sure to post some pics of my YJ and my buddie's '82 CJ7 in use (a la dirty) soon.  If ya ask me those BFG A/T's are the best all-around tires.  Me and Nik both have them on our jeeps, and the other Nick (yes spelled diff.) has them on his '98 F250 4x4 and they are smooth, relatively quiet, handle good, and provide plenty of grip even on very very loose soft dirt (read 35-degree angles in dirt you would sink to your ankles in) but unfortunately are not the best choice for serious mudding (although I did pull my buddy in his '89 T100 out of the mud with them-oh yeah, he's got BFG's too-just bald)<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">     <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!<P><A HREF="http://clubs.excite.com/welcome/main?cid=.zXb1DJ1lsCL&aid=22&auth=" TARGET=_blank>Pontiac Fiero Owner's Club</A>-Pics, Videos and More-Or Post your Own||||reg||1
